# Roboter Studio manual control — jog the REAL follower one step. Reuses the
# workflow trajectory path (quintic + velocity floor + the sole
# /leader/joint_trajectory publisher), so a jog is a bounded, velocity-safe move
# just like every workflow motion. Modes:
#   joint      — nudge arm joint `index` (0..4) or the gripper (index 5) by
#                `delta` rad; REFUSED (not silently clamped) if it exceeds the
#                Dynamixel limit / gripper band.
#   cartesian  — nudge the end-effector by `delta` m along X(0)/Y(1)/Z(2), or the
#                tool roll (index 3) by `delta` rad. Pitch/yaw (index >=4) is
#                rejected (the top-down arm cannot hold them).
#   drive_to   — move straight to (target_x, target_y, target_z), top-down roll
#                (the per-block „fahre dorthin" / the editor's Move button).
# `duration_s` is the REQUESTED move duration (clamped; the velocity floor may
# extend it). Torque is asserted ON at the start of the move.
string mode
int32 index
float32 delta
float32 target_x
float32 target_y
float32 target_z
float32 duration_s
---
bool success
float32[] joints
float32 world_x
float32 world_y
float32 world_z
string message
